<http://data.silknow.org/object/dda66874-7538-3d57-be73-5264e1e65987>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Skirt of brocaded silk, the skirt is unpicked, Spitalfields, England, 1743-1746"@en , "Part of a skirt made of woven silk. The silk has an off-white light taffeta ground (probably a lustring) and is brocaded in fresh colours with sprays of mixed flowers, some with passion flowers and some with carnations. The stems and leaves are brocaded in emerald, apple green and black.\n\nTechnique: Taffeta ground with brocaded wefts bound in 3\\1 twill by a proportion of the ground warp threads (1 in 6).\n\nSelvedges: Plain tabby."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/6aff667b-30c6-3845-b350-98f4f7524aa0> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Part of a skirt made of woven silk. The silk has an off-white light taffeta ground (probably a lustring) and is brocaded in fresh colours with sprays of mixed flowers, some with passion flowers and some with carnations. The stems and leaves are brocaded in emerald, apple green and black.\n\nTechnique: Taffeta ground with brocaded wefts bound in 3\\1 twill by a proportion of the ground warp threads (1 in 6).\n\nSelvedges: Plain tabby."@en , "Skirt of brocaded silk, the skirt is unpicked, Spitalfields, England, 1743-1746"@en ;
